{
  "id": "wifi-lab",
  "name": "WiFi Lab",
  "description": "HTB Academy-style WiFi Pentester range on VMware Workstation: a real hostapd access point on a passed-through Realtek RTL8188FU USB dongle (0bda:f179; open/WEP/WPA2/WPA3/WPS/hidden-SSID/MAC-filter/enterprise scenarios, switchable live), a second independent hostapd AP on a passed-through AltoBeam ATBM6012B-X USB dongle (007a:888b) for two-BSSID scenarios (evil-twin, real OWE-transition) the primary AP's single AP-mode radio can't do alone, a Kali GUI attacker with a passed-through USB WiFi adapter (MediaTek 0e8d:7610), FreeRADIUS for 802.1x/Enterprise scenarios, and a Wazuh SIEM that ingests the AP's hostapd journal so attacks show on a dashboard with MITRE ATT&CK tags. Needs three USB WiFi adapters plugged into the host. VirtualBox cannot pass the AltoBeam through (see docs/labs/wifi/altobeam), so this template uses VMware.",
